{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal record screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider may not ask about or consider an applicant's criminal record before making a conditional offer, and may never consider arrests without conviction, expunged, pardoned, vacated or sealed records, or juvenile adjudications.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider, except dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Housing provider may still inquire about methamphetamine manufacture or production convictions on federally assisted housing premises and whether the applicant is subject to a lifetime sex offender registration requirement.","coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"Monetary penalty up to $1,000 (no prior violation in five years), up to $5,000 (one prior), up to $10,000 (two or more priors); director may order other relief including return of the application fee and up to $1,000 to the applicant.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not require an applicant to complete any housing application that includes any inquiries regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to the provision of a conditional offer","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application fee disclosure","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether its eligibility criteria include criminal history review and that the applicant may present evidence of inaccuracies, rehabilitation or mitigating factors.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider, except dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"Monetary penalty up to $1,000 (no prior violation in five years), up to $5,000 (one prior), up to $10,000 (two or more priors); director may order the application fee returned.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1) Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Eviction of applicant placed by director's order after successful appeal","requirement":"If a court overturns the director's order on the housing provider's appeal, the provider may evict the former applicant who was placed in its unit by that order, giving at least 45 days' notice.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"A former applicant residing in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director's order under the act.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Applies only where the housing provider's appeal succeeds and a court overturns the director's final decision ordering the housing provider to house the applicant.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","n_rules":3,"note":null}

